  "cards": [
    {
      "title": "Capture boundaries",
      "items": [
        "Public protocol exchanges are observed after the handler; participating local SQL outcomes are captured with their mutation. The protocol library has no webhook transport dependency.",
        "Managed webhooks require SQL and encryption. Summary capture and sensitive representations have separate authorization."
      ],
      "dot": "policy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Delivery and replay",
      "items": [
        "Delivery is at least once and unordered. Consumers deduplicate delivery IDs; a replay creates a new delivery for the same occurrence.",
        "The worker retries failures using persistent leases and backoff. Subscription revision changes pause old backlog; replay cannot reconstruct representations that were not retained."
      ],
      "dot": "storage"
    },
    {
      "title": "Receiver authentication",
      "items": [
        "Requests carry Standard Webhooks signature headers. Receiver verification, replay-window checks and deduplication are separate from transport TLS."
      ],
      "dot": "authentication"
    },
    {
      "dot": "transport",
